<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  body { font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #222; background: #f7f7f7; margin: 0; padding: 20px; }
  h1 { font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 4px 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 28px 0 2px 0; }
  .subtitle { color: #666; font-size: 13px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; }
  .basis-note { font-size: 11px; color: #555; margin: 0 0 8px 0; }
  .basis-note.not-comparable { color: #7a4b00; background: #fff8e6; border: 1px solid #f0dca0; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 4px; display: inline-block; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; background: #fff; font-size: 12px; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 6px 8px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #2c3e50; color: #fff; }
  th.primary { background: #1a5276; }
  td.fee-label { font-weight: bold; background: #f0f3f5; white-space: nowrap; }
  tr.shared td.fee-label { background: #eaf2fb; }
  tr.shared { background: #f5faff; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .fee-value { display: block; }
  .fee-value + .fee-value { margin-top: 6px; padding-top: 6px; border-top: 1px dashed #ddd; }
  .scope { display: block; color: #888; font-size: 10px; font-style: italic; }
  .mechanism { display: block; color: #888; font-size: 10px; }
  .confidence-badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px; margin-top: 2px; }
  .confidence-low { background: #fdecea; color: #a94442; }
  .confidence-medium { background: #fff8e6; color: #7a4b00; }
  .mismatch-flag { display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: bold; color: #a94442; background: #fdecea; border: 1px solid #f3c8c4; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 3px; margin-left: 6px; }
  .drift-badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px; margin-top: 2px; background: #eaf2fb; color: #1a5276; }
  /* Asserted-universal: a written catch-all statement, not several
     independent scrapes agreeing -- kept visually distinct from a plain
     "verified across all products" scope so it's never mistaken for
     stronger evidence than it is. */
  .assertion-badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px; margin-top: 2px; background: #f3ecfb; color: #5b3a8e; }
  /* A flag with a confirmed track record of mostly being a false alarm is
     demoted to this muted style instead of being hidden -- still visible,
     just quieter, and the tooltip always shows the track record behind it. */
  .confidence-badge.demoted, .mismatch-flag.demoted, .drift-badge.demoted { background: #f0f0f0; color: #888; border-color: #e0e0e0; }
  /* Distinct from the generic low-confidence badge: this means regex/CSS-
     selector extraction found NOTHING at all, and an LLM fallback read
     the page instead -- a fundamentally different, weaker kind of
     uncertainty than "two matches on the page disagreed". */
  .llm-badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px; margin-top: 2px; background: #fff0e0; color: #a35a00; border: 1px solid #f0c896; }
  .llm-badge.demoted { background: #f0f0f0; color: #888; border-color: #e0e0e0; }
  .legend { font-size: 11px; color: #666; margin-top: 6px; }
  .legend .swatch { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; background: #eaf2fb; border: 1px solid #ddd; vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 4px; }
  .warnings { margin-top: 24px; }
  .warnings h2 { font-size: 15px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .warnings ul { font-size: 12px; color: #7a4b00; background: #fff8e6; border: 1px solid #f0dca0; padding: 12px 12px 12px 28px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .warnings li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .empty-note { color: #888; font-size: 12px; margin-top: 20px; }
  .not-stated { color: #aaa; font-style: italic; }
  .matrix-note { font-size: 11px; color: #555; margin: 0 0 8px 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>{{ subject }}</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Generated {{ generated_at }}. Columns for {{ primary_institution }} are highlighted in the header. Fees are grouped by product category -- see the note above each table for the comparison basis, and each value's italicized line for which specific product(s) it was verified for.</p>

  {% if credit_card_matrix %}
  <h2>Credit Card Comparison</h2>
  <p class="matrix-note">None of these institutions supports a clean per-card comparison (a shared agreement/disclosure covers multiple cards identically, or APR tiers don't map to card names) -- but every fee other than APR is confirmed identical across an institution's own card types, so credit cards are compared once per institution here rather than broken out by card tier. Where a secured card's APR genuinely differs from the general rate, or reward structure/promotions genuinely vary by card, that's shown as its own row or a per-card breakdown within the cell. Muted, greyed-out values (e.g. "Not stated") mean the available source doesn't address that fee at all -- that's different from a confirmed "None", which means the source affirmatively states there's no fee. Every figure in this table has been fact-checked directly against each institution's primary source (agreement PDF, disclosure, or live rate page) as of the date above; source URLs are on file rather than repeated inline here.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Fee</th>
        {% for inst in credit_card_matrix.institutions %}
        <th class="{{ 'primary' if inst == primary_institution else '' }}">{{ inst }}{% if loop.index0 in credit_card_matrix.issuer_columns %}<sup title="Every value in this column except Annual Fee/APR is set by this institution's card issuer -- see the footnote below.">&dagger;</sup>{% endif %}</th>
        {% endfor %}
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in credit_card_matrix.rows %}
      <tr>
        <td class="fee-label">{{ row.label }}</td>
        {% for cell in row.cells %}
        <td>
          {% if cell.not_publicly_disclosed %}
            <span>{{ cell.value }}<sup title="Set individually by this institution and disclosed only at account opening -- not publicly available. See the footnote below.">&Dagger;</sup></span>
          {% elif cell.muted %}
            <span class="not-stated">{{ cell.value }}</span>
          {% else %}
            {{ cell.value }}
          {% endif %}
          {% if cell.llm_assisted %}
            <span class="llm-badge" title="Normal pattern-matching found nothing on the source page; an AI fallback (Gemini) read the page instead. Not independently verified.">AI-extracted, unverified</span>
          {% endif %}
        </td>
        {% endfor %}
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if sections %}
  {% for section in sections %}
  <h2>{{ section.label }}</h2>
  <p class="basis-note{{ '' if section.comparable else ' not-comparable' }}">{{ section.basis_note }}</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Fee</th>
        {% for inst in section.institutions %}
        <th class="{{ 'primary' if inst == primary_institution else '' }}">{{ inst }}</th>
        {% endfor %}
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in section.rows %}
      <tr class="{{ 'shared' if row.shared else '' }}">
        <td class="fee-label">{{ row.label }}
          {% if row.mechanism_mismatch %}
          <span class="mismatch-flag{{ ' demoted' if row.mismatch_severity == 'demoted' else '' }}"
                title="These values use different fee mechanisms (e.g. flat vs. percentage vs. recurring) -- not a direct apples-to-apples comparison.{% if row.mismatch_stats %} Historically {{ row.mismatch_stats.false_alarms }}/{{ row.mismatch_stats.total }} confirmed false alarms for this flag on this fee.{% endif %}">&#9888; different fee types{% if row.mismatch_severity == 'demoted' %} (often not significant){% endif %}</span>
          {% endif %}
        </td>
        {% for cell in row.cells %}
        <td>
          {% if cell %}
            {% for entry in cell %}
            <span class="fee-value">{{ entry.value }}{% if entry.issuers %}<sup title="Set by the issuer ({{ entry.issuers|join(', ') }}), not by this institution directly -- see the footnote below.">&dagger;</sup>{% endif %}{% if entry.not_publicly_disclosed %}<sup title="Set individually by this institution and disclosed only at account opening -- not publicly available. See the footnote below.">&Dagger;</sup>{% endif %}<span class="scope">{{ entry.scope }}</span><span class="mechanism">{{ entry.mechanism_label }}</span>{% if entry.verification == "asserted" %}<span class="assertion-badge" title="Sourced from a written catch-all statement, not independently confirmed per product.{% if entry.source_quote %} Quote: &quot;{{ entry.source_quote }}&quot;{% endif %}{% if entry.source_locator %} ({{ entry.source_locator }}){% endif %}">asserted, not independently verified</span>{% endif %}{% if entry.confidence == "llm_assisted" %}<span class="llm-badge{{ ' demoted' if entry.confidence_severity == 'demoted' else '' }}" title="Normal pattern-matching found nothing on the source page; an AI fallback (Gemini) read the page instead. Not independently verified.{% if entry.confidence_stats %} Historically {{ entry.confidence_stats.false_alarms }}/{{ entry.confidence_stats.total }} confirmed false alarms for this flag on this fee.{% endif %}">AI-extracted, unverified{% if entry.confidence_severity == 'demoted' %} (often reliable so far){% endif %}</span>{% elif entry.confidence != "high" %}<span class="confidence-badge confidence-{{ entry.confidence }}{{ ' demoted' if entry.confidence_severity == 'demoted' else '' }}"{% if entry.confidence_stats %} title="Historically {{ entry.confidence_stats.false_alarms }}/{{ entry.confidence_stats.total }} confirmed false alarms for this flag on this fee."{% endif %}>{{ entry.confidence }} confidence{% if entry.confidence_severity == 'demoted' %} (often a false alarm){% endif %}</span>{% endif %}{% if entry.changed %}<span class="drift-badge{{ ' demoted' if entry.drift_severity == 'demoted' else '' }}"{% if entry.drift_stats %} title="Historically {{ entry.drift_stats.false_alarms }}/{{ entry.drift_stats.total }} confirmed false alarms for this flag on this fee."{% endif %}>changed since last snapshot &mdash; was: {{ entry.previous_value }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
            {% endfor %}
          {% else %}
            &mdash;
          {% endif %}
        </td>
        {% endfor %}
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  {% if section.comparable %}
  <p class="legend"><span class="swatch"></span>Rows shaded like this appear for 2 or more institutions in this category &mdash; the closest fee-for-fee comparisons available today.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty-note">No card data was available for this run.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {% if warnings %}
  <div class="warnings">
    <h2>Data Quality Notes</h2>
    <ul>
      {% for warning in warnings %}
      <li>{{ warning }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if used_issuer_footnote or used_not_disclosed_footnote %}
  <p class="empty-note">
    {% if used_issuer_footnote %}&dagger; Issued by a third-party issuer on the institution's behalf. Fees are set by the issuer and are what this institution's cardholders pay.<br>{% endif %}
    {% if used_not_disclosed_footnote %}&Dagger; Set individually by this institution and disclosed only at account opening; not publicly available.{% endif %}
  </p>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="empty-note">Spotted a wrong value or a badge that's a false alarm? Add a verdict to data/feedback_log.yaml -- confirmed corrections are added to the shared fee-name taxonomy for every institution, and repeated false-alarm verdicts quiet that flag type down in future reports.</p>
</body>
</html>
